    <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
            <p class="sec-sub">Real questions Mumbai logistics + courier + freight operators ask us.</p>
            <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;">
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Which is bigger for logistics marketing in Mumbai &mdash; JNPT/freight forwarding or Bhiwandi/3PL?</h3><div class="faq-a">Both are large but serve different buyers. JNPT-focused freight forwarding is a bigger revenue segment (single-shipment values Rs 5 lakh-Rs 5 Cr) but with longer cycles + smaller buyer pool. Bhiwandi-focused 3PL + fulfilment has higher account volume + faster cycles + growing D2C brand ecosystem. Most Mumbai marketing budgets get better ROI on Bhiwandi 3PL D2C in year 1 + then expand to JNPT-focused enterprise ABM in year 2.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How do Mumbai courier operators compete with Blue Dart + Delhivery for corporate accounts?</h3><div class="faq-a">Not on brand + national-network parity. Win on: hyper-local knowledge of BKC + Andheri + Colaba pickup + delivery windows, corporate-account service SLAs (2-hour pickup, guaranteed same-day within Mumbai), WhatsApp responsiveness for HR + admin teams, and specialised service tiers (high-value insured, cold-chain samples, cross-border documents). Category leadership on corporate-corridor service beats national-brand competition.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">What is a realistic marketing budget for a Mumbai-based 3PL operator?</h3><div class="faq-a">Rs 2-4 lakh / month all-in for founder-led ops (Rs 10-50 Cr revenue). Rs 5-15 lakh / month for mid-market (Rs 50-500 Cr, multi-city). Rs 15-40 lakh+ for enterprise + multi-region (Rs 500 Cr+). Mumbai's D2C brand density + Bhiwandi capacity make even smaller operators competitive on well-executed budgets.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Are there specific Mumbai regulations we should market compliance around?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes. Maharashtra GST on freight + logistics, MMRDA transport permits + timing restrictions for goods vehicles in Mumbai (10 pm - 5 am windows for HGV), Bhiwandi warehousing compliance (fire safety, structural, MPCB), JNPT customs + ICD registration. Compliance content targeted at these ranks well because Mumbai + Maharashtra-specific.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Should Mumbai freight forwarders publish content on Cargo Talk vs LinkedIn?</h3><div class="faq-a">Both. Cargo Talk placements build category authority + PR-worthy signal for enterprise buyers evaluating vendors. LinkedIn founder + leadership content builds warm-up for Sales Nav ABM. Different roles; both compound. 6-10 Cargo Talk / trade-pub placements + 2-3 LinkedIn posts / week is the Growth-tier cadence.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How does Mumbai's D2C brand ecosystem affect 3PL marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Materially. Mumbai + Maharashtra is home to Sugar, Mamaearth, boAt, WOW, Purplle, Nykaa (offices), MyGlamm, Bella Vita, hundreds of mid-cap D2C fashion + beauty brands. Any 3PL marketing must reference these brand-adjacencies, solve for their peak-season patterns (Diwali, EOSS, Rakshabandhan), and speak to their integration + rate + support standards. Generic 3PL messaging fails against operators who lead with brand-specific case studies.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Should we build a Mumbai-only marketing programme or expand to India-wide from day one?</h3><div class="faq-a">Mumbai-only for the first 12-18 months if you serve exclusively Mumbai + Maharashtra. India-wide from day one only if you have multi-city operational capacity + revenue justification. Marketing efficiency compounds on tight geographic focus; premature expansion dilutes both spend + operational quality.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Do you help Mumbai operators with GCC expansion?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes. Many Mumbai-based freight forwarders + international couriers serve India-to-UAE + India-to-KSA lanes. We run GCC + India dual-market campaigns for logistics + adjacent categories. English + Hindi + Arabic creative production, INR + AED + SAR pricing narratives, region-specific GBPs for Dubai + Sharjah + Riyadh hubs. See our related freight-forwarding + international-courier playbooks.</div></div>
            </div>
